xcheck 1
# Section 7 row: "search effort" (core: SearchLimits, 20000 steps and 32 backend checks;
# libliftoff: a deadline, raised by the harness, which records whether it was reached).
# Ten planes, ids 50..59, zpos 0..15, zpos_now = index. Only plane 50 (the primary) lists NV12.
# Frames, model setting, predicted class (all INFERRED; nothing has been run):
#   ten-argb-layers          both-accept (control, first fit).
#   nv12-lowest-nine-argb    both-accept (control: the NV12 layer is lowest and goes to plane 50,
#                            the AR24 layers fill planes 51..59).
#   eight-argb-two-nv12-late both-reject in outcome. Two NV12 layers for one NV12 plane cannot be
#                            placed. Core: either a quick NoPlane or, if it explores the
#                            permutations of the first eight layers before reaching the late
#                            failure (about 9P8 = 362880 nodes), core-error(LimitExceeded).
#                            UNCERTAIN which; libliftoff: partial placement, the deadline flag
#                            may be set. The row's liftoff-only class is not expected here.
# The frames overlap fully, so the zpos relation matters, but the plane order matches.
